{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices"}]},{"type":"text","text":" are the kept vertices in the base’s order, at view indices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":": the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"view keeps two arrays, base index to view index and back, so a row is the base’s row filtered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and renumbered with one array load per entry and no hashing. A spanning subgraph keeps every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex at its base index."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Edges","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" keep the base’s positions, so a weight closure keyed by the base’s positions works","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on the view. An edge is in the view when both its ends are, and, if an edge set was given,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when it is in the set. With an edge set the view has dense edge indices: an edge’s index is its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rank among the kept edges in base order. Over a base with edge indices the set is a bit mask","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a count per 64-bit word, so the rank costs one popcount. Over a base without them (an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a complement, an induced subgraph) the set is the sorted kept positions, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a row entry or a rank costs a binary search. An induced subgraph has no edge indices: building","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its edge mask would cost O(m).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The view holds a copy of the base (value semantics), so mutating the original never shows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through. Phase 1 needs a base with vertex indices; a "},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with vertex holes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"traps at construction."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"densely. Made by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inducedSubgraph(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spanningSubgraph(edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph(vertices:edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph_view"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsSubgraph"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SubDigraph"},{"type":"text","text":", Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"filtered_graph"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges"],"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations"]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"GraphOperations"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","